    "body": "> it'll initially inherit my service worker via this step, but will discard it during navigation?\r\n\r\nRight.\r\n\r\n> If the target origin doesn't have a service worker, when is the active worker set to null?\r\n\r\nthe environment settings object's active service worker is copied from the reserved client's active service worker in this case. And the reserved client's active service worker should have gotten a service worker from the registration matching in Handle Fetch. So, the active service worker's value here's an initial value of the reserved client (an environment's) [active service worker](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-environment-active-service-worker). Not sure if we still need \"It is initially null.\" sentence.",
